experiment: slotdose
  the question      §53. §52's pre-registered primary cleared 2 SE mostly
                    because its CONTROL went negative (79% of it at 900k).
                    Why did the control move? Measured, not re-run.
  the method        the formant gap splits EXACTLY into a SLOT TERM -- all a
                    per-context bias table can produce -- and an OBJECT
                    RESIDUAL, which it cannot. No new mechanism, no new genome
                    field, no core change: instrumentation only.
  the hypothesis    UNEQUAL DOSE. The untaught voice already sits 30% of the
                    way toward /a/ (G = +0.4950 of 1.6417), so a 50/50
                    compromise LOWERS G -- and the more-written slot is pulled
                    further. Predicts sign(dG) = -sign(d dose). SIGN DERIVED.
  session           900.0 s of simulated life x 120 sessions, 4 arms
  instrument        slotdose   trial seed 0000000001357469   120 sessions
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)

  CLAUSE 0 -- LIVENESS AND IDENTIFICATION, read on EVERY arm including the
  one whose null is load-bearing. A creature with != 2 live slots is DROPPED
  from the cell columns; the residual needs all four cells populated.
    T1.RET       n 36/36  dropped 0  present 1.0000  occ 0.5392  4-cell 23/36  median |d dose| 0.1324
    T1.RET.D     n 36/36  dropped 0  present 1.0000  occ 0.5347  4-cell 23/36  median |d dose| 0.2863
    T1.ORACLE.D  n 36/36  dropped 0  present 1.0000  occ 0.5035  4-cell 0/36  median |d dose| 0.1898
    T1.ORACLE    n 12/12  dropped 0  present 1.0000  occ 0.5035  4-cell 0/12  median |d dose| 0.2054

  THE MIXTURE -- H's PREMISE, TESTED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. Fraction of each
  slot's lessons that taught kWords[1] /i/. A DRAWN arm must read ~0.50 in
  BOTH slots (that is what makes it label-destroyed); a PAIRED arm must not.
    T1.RET       slot A 0.1538   slot B 0.8113   (paired)
    T1.RET.D     slot A 0.4992   slot B 0.5000   (drawn: both -> 0.50)
    T1.ORACLE.D  slot A 0.4847   slot B 0.4996   (drawn: both -> 0.50)
    T1.ORACLE    slot A 0.0000   slot B 1.0000   (paired)

  THE WORD PREFERENCE, G = perr(cube) - perr(ball), POSITIVE = NEARER /a/.
  `echo G` is the untaught reference measured in this run. Slot A is the one
  object 0 over-occupies, so sign(slot term) = sign(G_A - G_B) by construction.
    T1.RET       G_A +0.5089  G_B +0.5309  G_A-G_B -0.0220  mean G +0.5192  echo G +0.5021
    T1.RET.D     G_A +0.4748  G_B +0.6106  G_A-G_B -0.1358  mean G +0.5555  echo G +0.5021
    T1.ORACLE.D  G_A +0.5361  G_B +0.5024  G_A-G_B +0.0337  mean G +0.5200  echo G +0.5021
    T1.ORACLE    G_A +0.6954  G_B +0.4773  G_A-G_B +0.2181  mean G +0.5892  echo G +0.4896

  THE DECOMPOSITION. `gap` is §52's primary rebuilt from the cells and must
  reproduce the `pe` column beside it. `identity` is gap - (slot + residual)
  and is ARITHMETIC: anything but zero is a bookkeeping error of mine.
    T1.RET       gap +0.0233 +- 0.0193  (pe +0.0233)   SLOT +0.0081 +- 0.0170   RESIDUAL +0.0152   identity +1.11e-16
    T1.RET.D     gap -0.0868 +- 0.0304  (pe -0.0868)   SLOT -0.0947 +- 0.0306   RESIDUAL +0.0079   identity -8.33e-17
    T1.ORACLE.D  gap +0.0211 +- 0.0327  (pe +0.0211)   SLOT +0.0211 +- 0.0327   RESIDUAL +0.0000   identity +3.82e-17
    T1.ORACLE    gap +0.1293 +- 0.0478  (pe +0.1293)   SLOT +0.1293 +- 0.0478   RESIDUAL +0.0000   identity -2.78e-17

  THE REPRODUCTION COLUMN -- this log's own proof that the instrument did
  not move the session. §52's drop rule, every scored creature, so these
  must equal §52's formant-gap column at the same budget TO FOUR DECIMALS
  INCLUDING THE SE. (The cell columns above drop != 2-live-slot creatures and
  so run on a subset; this one does not.)
    T1.RET       formant gap +0.0233 +- 0.0193  (n 36)
    T1.RET.D     formant gap -0.0868 +- 0.0304  (n 36)
    T1.ORACLE.D  formant gap +0.0211 +- 0.0327  (n 36)
    T1.ORACLE    formant gap +0.1293 +- 0.0478  (n 12)

  T-A -- THE BOOKKEEPING SELF-TEST. A PINNED index makes the cells exactly
  diagonal, so T1.ORACLE's residual must be EXACTLY zero and its slot term
  must equal its gap. Worst identity over all 120 creatures +1.11e-16.
    identity zero everywhere  PASS
    ORACLE residual zero      PASS (+0.00e+00)

  T-E -- REGISTRATION. Is the lesson read back from the slot it was WRITTEN
  to? The modal slot per object over the TEACHING windows against the modal
  slot per object over the PROBES. NOTHING IN §49-§52 CAN SEE THIS:
  `vis_ctx_match` maximises over slot permutations, so a perfectly SWAPPED
  index scores exactly what an aligned one does. The pinned arms must read
  100% aligned -- that is a self-test, not a result.
    T1.RET       aligned 36  SWAPPED  0  degenerate  0   (100% aligned)
    T1.RET.D     aligned 36  SWAPPED  0  degenerate  0   (100% aligned)
    T1.ORACLE.D  aligned 36  SWAPPED  0  degenerate  0   (100% aligned)
    T1.ORACLE    aligned 12  SWAPPED  0  degenerate  0   (100% aligned)
    pinned arms 0% swapped   PASS

  AND THE SPLIT, PRE-REGISTERED WITH ITS DIRECTION BEFORE IT WAS READ: if a
  swap is reading the lesson out of the wrong slot, then within the PAIRED
  derived arm the ALIGNED creatures read POSITIVE and the SWAPPED ones
  NEGATIVE. Registration is scored off the slot histograms and never off G,
  so conditioning on it is not fitting the verdict to the data.
    T1.RET       ALIGNED G_A-G_B -0.0220 +- 0.0336 gap +0.0233 (n 36)   SWAPPED G_A-G_B +0.0000 +- 0.0000 gap +0.0000 (n  0)
    T1.RET.D     ALIGNED G_A-G_B -0.1358 +- 0.0501 gap -0.0868 (n 36)   SWAPPED G_A-G_B +0.0000 +- 0.0000 gap +0.0000 (n  0)
    T1.ORACLE.D  ALIGNED G_A-G_B +0.0337 +- 0.0520 gap +0.0211 (n 36)   SWAPPED G_A-G_B +0.0000 +- 0.0000 gap +0.0000 (n  0)
    T1.ORACLE    ALIGNED G_A-G_B +0.2181 +- 0.0778 gap +0.1293 (n 12)   SWAPPED G_A-G_B +0.0000 +- 0.0000 gap +0.0000 (n  0)

  T-B -- THE PRIMARY, A PAIRED SIGN TEST ON T1.RET.D. Per creature, does
  sign(G_A - G_B) OPPOSE sign(dose_A - dose_B)? Bar >=26 of 36 (p = 0.0057).
    T1.RET       oppose 15  agree 21  tied  0
    T1.RET.D     oppose 15  agree 21  tied  0
    T1.ORACLE.D  oppose 17  agree 19  tied  0
    T1.ORACLE    oppose  9  agree  3  tied  0

  T-C -- THE SHARE. How much of T1.RET.D's displacement the slot route
  accounts for, and the per-creature regressions of gap on the two
  imbalances. H predicts NEGATIVE on both.
    slot term -0.0947 of gap -0.0868 = 109% of it
    slope d gap / d FIRING dose +0.3534 +- 0.0848 (4.2 SE)
    slope d gap / d OCCUPANCY   +0.4934 +- 0.0956 (5.2 SE)

  §53b -- THE SLOT TERM AT ZERO IMBALANCE. §53 measured the confound's slope
  at +5.2 SE and the two derived arms carrying DIFFERENT amounts of it, so it
  does not cancel in their difference. Each arm's per-creature slot term is
  regressed on its SIGNED occupancy imbalance and read at zero. The signed
  means are printed because §53 printed only medians of |.| and had to infer
  the sign from a regression instead of reading it off.
  DISCLOSED: a MEASURED covariate, not a randomised one -- an adjustment under
  a linearity assumption it cannot verify, printed BESIDE the raw term.
    T1.RET       mean occ imb +0.0301 (SD 0.1472)  mean dose imb -0.0227 | RAW slot +0.0081 +- 0.0170 | slope +0.4465 +- 0.0908  ADJUSTED -0.0053 +- 0.0135 (-0.4 SE)
    T1.RET.D     mean occ imb -0.0743 (SD 0.2448)  mean dose imb -0.1651 | RAW slot -0.0947 +- 0.0306 | slope +0.5223 +- 0.0925  ADJUSTED -0.0559 +- 0.0234 (-2.4 SE)
    T1.ORACLE.D  mean occ imb +0.0025 (SD 0.2450)  mean dose imb +0.0096 | RAW slot +0.0211 +- 0.0327 | slope +0.5113 +- 0.1057  ADJUSTED +0.0198 +- 0.0255 (0.8 SE)
    T1.ORACLE    mean occ imb +0.0314 (SD 0.1843)  mean dose imb -0.0146 | RAW slot +0.1293 +- 0.0478 | slope +0.5566 +- 0.2230  ADJUSTED +0.1118 +- 0.0400 (2.8 SE)

    PREDICTION 1 (SELF-TEST): T1.ORACLE.D's adjusted term within 2 SE of
    zero -- PASS (+0.0198 +- 0.0255, 0.8 SE), on a regressor with SD 0.2450 so the
    test is IDENTIFIED and could have failed. A pinned label-destroyed arm
    has nothing to express at equal occupancy; a non-zero value would mean
    the adjustment is MIS-SPECIFIED and nothing in §53b could be quoted.
    (DISCLOSED: at 150k this same arm reads SD 0.0126 and the test is void
    by construction there, which is why the branch measures rather than
    asserts.)

    THE LINEARITY CHECK, WHICH CAN FAIL: T1.RET.D split at its median
    imbalance gives slopes +0.6411 +- 0.2109 (low) and +0.6558 +- 0.1829 (high),
    differing by 0.1 SE -- CONSISTENT: a linear adjustment is supported

    PREDICTION 2: T1.RET.D's displacement at zero imbalance -0.0559 +- 0.0234 -- STILL NON-ZERO: the confound is PARTIAL and this is the size of what survives
    PREDICTION 3: T1.RET's lesson estimate -0.0053 +- 0.0135, against §53's
    bracket of +0.046 (21% of the ceiling) and +0.114 (66%, write purity).
    The pinned ceiling on the SAME footing is +0.1118 +- 0.0400 (adjusted, its regressor identified), so this
    is -5% of it.

    AND THE ADJUSTMENT'S POSITIVE CONTROL: the same correction applied to
    the PINNED arm leaves +0.1118 of its raw +0.1293 -- 86% retained, 2.8 SE
    above zero. So the correction is NOT a blunt shrink toward zero: it
    keeps a real lesson where there is one and removes the derived arm's.
    The ceiling clears 2 SE after adjustment, so the null above is INFORMATIVE.

  THE VERDICT.

    (4b) NO VERDICT ON H: oppose 15, agree 21 of 36, neither at the bar of
    26. The decomposition still stands on its own and is the result:
    slot -0.0947 +- 0.0306, residual +0.0079.

